From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] liblog: the logd writer prints info and worse to stderr

The translated guest's liblog (/system/lib64/arm64/liblog.so, run by the native bridge) writes to logd, which does not exist on the desktop, and has no logger hook
installed by the host (bridge/native/android_platform.c installs it in the host-side liblog only), so a guest library's log lines were lost (Fennec's Gecko under x86
translation). The logd writer now also prints info and worse (Unity's own graphics API lines are INFO), and everything with the property debug.apklayer.log=1 (the guest's environment hides APKLAYER_*),
to fd 2 as `[log N] tag: message`, the host hook's format. Where the host's hook is installed it replaces this writer. Module liblog.

diff --git a/liblog/logger_write.cpp b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
--- a/liblog/logger_write.cpp
+++ b/liblog/logger_write.cpp
@@ -347,6 +347,16 @@
   vec[1].iov_len = strlen(log_message->tag) + 1;
   vec[2].iov_base = const_cast<void*>(static_cast<const void*>(log_message->message));
   vec[2].iov_len = strlen(log_message->message) + 1;
+  // apklayer patch: no logd on the desktop; info and worse (all with the property debug.apklayer.log=1: the guest's environment hides APKLAYER_*)
+  // go to stderr as the host liblog's logger does
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  char all[PROP_VALUE_MAX] = {};
+  if (log_message->priority >= ANDROID_LOG_INFO || (__system_property_get("debug.apklayer.log", all) > 0 && all[0] == '1')) {
+    char line[1200];
+    int n = snprintf(line, sizeof(line), "[log %d] %s: %s\n", log_message->priority, log_message->tag, log_message->message);
+    if (n > 0) (void)!write(2, line, n < (int)sizeof(line) ? n : sizeof(line) - 1);
+  }
+#endif
 
   write_to_log(static_cast<log_id_t>(buffer_id), vec, 3, timestamp);
 }
